==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{rhymes|ɜː(ɹ)vi}}

===Etymology===
* Noun usage from the adjective {{term|scurvy#Adjective|scurvy}} influenced by or a variant of {{term|scurfy}}. Took on meaning of {{etyl|nl}} {{term|scheurbuik|lang=nl}}, {{etyl|fr}} {{term|scorbut||scurvy|lang=fr}}, possibly from {{etyl|non}} {{term|skyrbjúgr|lang=non}}, {{term|skyr||sour milk}} + {{term|bjúgr||swelling, tumour}} whence the Icelandic {{term|skyrbjúgur||scurvy|lang=is}}. Compare German {{term|scharbock|lang=de}}, Late Latin {{term|scorbutus|lang=la}}.
* Alternate etymology is, from {{etyl|dum}}, from {{etyl|gml}}.

===Noun===
{{en-noun|-|scurvies}}

# {{disease}} A disease caused by insufficient intake of [[vitamin C]] leading to the formation of livid spots on the skin, spongy gums, loosening of the teeth and bleeding into the skin and from almost all mucous membranes.

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|vitamin C deficiency disease}} [[Barlow's disease]], [[Cheadle-Möller-Barlow syndrome]], [[Cheadle's disease]], [[Moeller's disease]], [[Möller-Barlow disease]], [[scorbutus]]

